        "text": "Okay, so I need to express the statement \"There exists exactly one number that is both prime and even\" in predicate logic using P(x) for \"x is prime\" and E(x) for \"x is even. Then, I have to prove whether this statement is true or false in the domain of positive integers. Hmm, let me break this down step by step."
      },
      {
        "label": "adding-knowledge",
        "text": "First, let's recall what predicate logic is. It's a formal system in logic that uses predicates, quantifiers, variables, and so on to make statements about objects. In this case, our objects are numbers, and the predicates are P(x) and E(x)."
