        "text": "The exact wording is \"There exists exactly one number that is both prime and even.\" So, in predicate logic, that should be:\n\n∃x (P(x) ∧ E(x)) ∧ ∀y (P(y) ∧ E(y) → y = x)"
      },
      {
        "label": "adding-knowledge",
        "text": "But actually, in standard logic, the existence of exactly one is usually expressed using two parts: existence and uniqueness."
