        "text": "Therefore, the only number that is both prime and even is 2. So, in the domain of positive integers, there exists exactly one number (which is 2) that is both prime and even.\n\nTherefore, the statement \"There exists exactly one number that is both prime and even\" is true in the domain of positive integers."
