o (1,1,2). From (1,1,2), I can go to (1,1,3). From (1,1,3), I can go to (1,1,4). But that's a dead end. So, maybe I need to find another path.\n\nWait, perhaps I should consider other moves from (1,1,1). Wait, no, from (1,1,1), the only available move is to (1,1,2). So, that's the only path.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I'm missing something. Let me think again.\n\nWait, perhaps I can move in a different direction. From (1,1,1), can I move to (1,2,1)? But (1,2,1) is blocked because x=2. Similarly, (2,1,1) is blocked because x=2. So, no, only (1,1,2) is available.\n\nSo, perhaps I need to find another way to reach (4,4,4). Maybe by moving in the x, y, or z direction.\n\nWait, let's try a different approach. Maybe I can move along the x-axis first.\n\nFrom (1,1,1), move to (2,1,1). But (2,1,1) is blocked because x=2. So, can't do that.\n\nAlternatively, move to (1,2,1), which is blocked. So, no.\n\nWait, so maybe I need to move in the z-direction first.\n\nFrom (1,1,1), move to (1,1,2). Then, from (1,1,2), move to (1,1,3). Then, from (1,1,3), move to (1,1,4). But that's a dead end.\n\nAlternatively, from (1,1,3), can I move to (1,2,3)? But (1,2,3) is blocked because y=2. So, no.\n\nWait, maybe I need to move in the y-direction.\n\nFrom (1,1,1), move to (1,2,1), which is blocked. So, no.\n\nAlternatively, move to (1,1,2). Then, from (1,1,2), move to (1,2,2), which is blocked because y=2. So, no.\n\nWait, so perhaps I need to find another path.\n\nWait, maybe I can move to (1,1,2), then to (1,2,2), but that's blocked. So, no.\n\nAlternatively, from (1,1,2), can I move to (2,1,2)? That's blocked because x=2. So, no.\n\nWait, so maybe I need to go back to (1,1,1) and try a different route.\n\nWait, but from (1,1,1), the only move is to (1,1,2). So, perhaps I need to find another way to reach (4,4,4) without getting stuck.\n\nWait, maybe I can move in the z-direction first.\n\nFrom (1,1,1), move to (1,1,2). Then, from (1,1,2), move to (1,1,3). Then, from (1,1,3), move to (1,1,4