ntal design.\n\nSo, conclusion for (a): Dr. Martinez specializes in neuroscience and has expertise in both statistics and computer programming? Wait, no. Wait, stats doesn't require programming, but stats requires experimental design. So, he's in stats and experimental design, but not necessarily in programming.\n\nWait, but he can't be in programming because he can't analyze large datasets. So, he must be in stats and experimental design.\n\nSo, conclusion for (a): Dr. Martinez specializes in neuroscience and has expertise in both statistics and computer programming? Wait, no. Wait, stats doesn't require programming, but stats requires experimental design. So, he's in stats and experimental design, but not necessarily in programming.\n\nWait, but he can't be in programming because he can't analyze large datasets. So, he must be in stats and experimental design.\n\nSo, conclusion for (a): Dr. Martinez specializes in neuroscience and has expertise in both statistics and computer programming? Wait, no. Wait, stats doesn't require programming, but stats requires experimental design. So, he's in stats and experimental design, but not necessarily in programming.\n\nWait, but he can't be in programming because he can't analyze large datasets. So, he must be in stats and experimental design.\n\nSo, conclusion for (a): Dr. Martinez specializes in neuroscience and has expertise in both statistics and computer programming? Wait, no. Wait, stats doesn't require programming, but stats requires experimental design. So, he's in stats and experimental design, but not necessarily in programming.\n\nWait, but he can't be in programming because he can't analyze large datasets. So, he must be in stats and experimental design.\n\nSo, conclusion for (a): Dr. Martinez specializes in neuroscience and has expertise in both statistics and computer programming? Wait, no. Wait, stats doesn't require programming, but stats requires experimental design. So, he's in stats and experimental design, but not necessarily in programming.",
